  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Using the Factor Theorem, fully factorise each of the following cubics:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^3-x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x(x-1)(x+1)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(0)&=0\\\\P(x)&=x(x^2-1)\\\\P(x)&=x(x-1)(x+1).\\end{align*}$$\nBy the Factor Theorem, $P(0)=0$ gives the factor $x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^3+3x^2+2x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x(x+1)(x+2)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3+3x^2+2x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(0)&=0\\\\P(x)&=x(x^2+3x+2)\\\\P(x)&=x(x+1)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$\nBy the Factor Theorem, $P(0)=0$ gives the factor $x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$-2x^3-2x^2+4x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-2x(x-1)(x+2)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=-2x^3-2x^2+4x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(0)&=0\\\\P(x)&=-2x(x^2+x-2)\\\\P(x)&=-2x(x-1)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$\nBy the Factor Theorem, $P(0)=0$ gives the factor $x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$-4x^3-24x^2-32x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-4x(x+2)(x+4)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=-4x^3-24x^2-32x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(0)&=0\\\\P(x)&=-4x(x^2+6x+8)\\\\P(x)&=-4x(x+2)(x+4).\\end{align*}$$\nBy the Factor Theorem, $P(0)=0$ gives the factor $x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x^3+6x^2+11x+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3+6x^2+11x+6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-1)&=-1+6-11+6\\\\P(-1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the Factor Theorem, $x+1$ is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(x^2+5x+6)\\\\P(x)&=(x+1)(x+2)(x+3).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$x^3-7x+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(x-2)(x+3)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-7x+6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1-7+6\\\\P(1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the Factor Theorem, $x-1$ is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(x^2+x-6)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(x-2)(x+3).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$x^3+3x^2-10x-24$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+2)(x-3)(x+4)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3+3x^2-10x-24$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-2)&=-8+12+20-24\\\\P(-2)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the Factor Theorem, $x+2$ is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+2)(x^2+x-12)\\\\P(x)&=(x+2)(x-3)(x+4).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$x^3-7x^2+16x-12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-2)^2(x-3)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-7x^2+16x-12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(2)&=8-28+32-12\\\\P(2)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the Factor Theorem, $x-2$ is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-2)(x^2-5x+6)\\\\P(x)&=(x-2)(x-2)(x-3)\\\\P(x)&=(x-2)^2(x-3).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$x^3+4x^2-3x-18$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+3)^2(x-2)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3+4x^2-3x-18$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(2)&=8+16-6-18\\\\P(2)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the Factor Theorem, $x-2$ is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-2)(x^2+6x+9)\\\\P(x)&=(x-2)(x+3)^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$3x^3-3x^2-15x-9$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3(x+1)^2(x-3)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=3x^3-3x^2-15x-9$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-1)&=-3-3+15-9\\\\P(-1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the Factor Theorem, $x+1$ is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(3x^2-6x-9)\\\\P(x)&=3(x+1)(x^2-2x-3)\\\\P(x)&=3(x+1)^2(x-3).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
